# Basic Concepts and Terminology

This page introduces the basic concepts and terminology used in the `@tanstack/react-form` library. Familiarizing yourself with these concepts will help you better understand and work with the library.

---

## Form Options

You can create options for your form so that it can be shared between multiple forms by using the `formOptions` function.

```tsx
interface User {
  firstName: string
  lastName: string
  hobbies: Array<string>
}
const defaultUser: User = { firstName: '', lastName: '', hobbies: [] }

const formOpts = formOptions({
  defaultValues: defaultUser,
})
```

---

## Form Instance

A Form Instance is an object that represents an individual form and provides methods and properties for working with the form.

```tsx
const form = useForm({
  ...formOpts,
  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {
    console.log(value)
  },
})
```

Alternatively, without `formOptions`:

```tsx
const form = useForm({
  defaultValues: defaultUser,
  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {
    console.log(value)
  },
})
```

---

## Field

A Field represents a single form input element.

```tsx
<form.Field
  name="firstName"
  children={(field) => (
    <>
      <input
        value={field.state.value}
        onBlur={field.handleBlur}
        onChange={(e) => field.handleChange(e.target.value)}
      />
      <FieldInfo field={field} />
    </>
  )}
/>
```

---

## Field State

```tsx
const {
  value,
  meta: { errors, isValidating },
} = field.state
```

```tsx
const { isTouched, isPristine, isDirty } = field.state.meta
```

> **Note**: `isDirty` in TanStack Form behaves differently than in React Hook Form.

---

## Field API

```tsx
<input
  value={field.state.value}
  onBlur={field.handleBlur}
  onChange={(e) => field.handleChange(e.target.value)}
/>
```

---

## Validation

Both sync and async validation are supported via the `validators` prop:

```tsx
<form.Field
  name="firstName"
  validators={{
    onChange: ({ value }) =>
      !value
        ? 'A first name is required'
        : value.length < 3
          ? 'First name must be at least 3 characters'
          : undefined,
    onChangeAsync: async ({ value }) => {
      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 1000))
      return value.includes('error') && 'No "error" allowed in first name'
    },
  }}
  children={(field) => (
    <>
      <input
        value={field.state.value}
        onBlur={field.handleBlur}
        onChange={(e) => field.handleChange(e.target.value)}
      />
      <FieldInfo field={field} />
    </>
  )}
/>
```

